+## Amendments to the spec, decided 2026-09-05 after lanes P and S merged (main = `797bca1`, v1.1.1)
+
+These override the spec where they differ. Each one was checked against the real code before this plan was written.
+
+| # | Spec said | Reality / decision |
+|---|---|---|
+| A-1 | §3.3 "`setWidth` has new logic: push Clear for lanes leaving the slot" | Already done by lane S (`NotchController.cpp:44-60`). Only the `WidthChange` reason is added. |
+| A-2 | §3.3 names the event flush `flushOutbox()` | That name already exists for the **command** outbox (`NotchController.cpp:688`). The event flush is `flushEventOutbox()`. |
+| A-3 | §3.1 "`~MainComponent` calls `setEventSink(nullptr)` before everything else" | That would drop the events `stop()` flushes (spec test 11). Order is: stop every controller (flushes to the sink → logger) → `sessionLogger_.stop()` (writes `session_end`) → detach sinks → `engine_.stop()`. |
+| A-4 | §3.3 `NotchEvent` carries `ctx` as fixed arrays, "memcpy, no alloc" | 3 × 1025 floats × 64 slots × 2 vectors × 8 controllers ≈ 12 MB resident. The detector thread already allocates per block (`std::vector<double> locked` in `processSpectrumForDetection`), so `ctx` is a `std::shared_ptr<const SpectralContext>` allocated only when a detector placement happens. The outbox cap (64) and drop counter stay. |
+| A-5 | §3.1 `SessionLogger::Config { directory, keepFiles }` in the constructor | The directory is chosen at `start()` (tests use a temp dir, the app uses `%APPDATA%`), so `start (directory, header)`; `keepFiles` stays a constructor argument. File name gets a millisecond suffix so five sessions started within one second never collide. |
+| A-6 | D-8 "`main.cpp` calls `setAppVersion (JUCE_APPLICATION_VERSION_STRING)`" | Nothing of the sort exists; `main.cpp:16` returns the hardcoded `"1.0.0"`. Task 6 adds `setAppVersion` AND fixes `getApplicationVersion()` to use the macro. |
+| A-7 | §4 test 8 "force the partial-apply unwind through a lane-1 sample-rate failure" | `setNotch` validates against `lanes_[0]`'s sample rate for every lane, so no input can make lane 1 alone fail. A TEST-ONLY hook `failNextSetNotchOnLaneForTest (int lane)` forces it. |
+| A-8 | §3.4 VERDICT column after STATUS, STATUS shrinks; existing column test pins 360 px | With a 92 px VERDICT column, HELD has 4 px at 360. The narrowest width the app ever gives the panel is 0.44 × (1200 − 24) ≈ 517 px. The column-budget test moves to 440 px (still below the real floor) — see Task 5. |
+| A-9 | Lane S loose ends: `loadPreset` never calls `slotPanel_.refresh()`; `adoptPreset` drops a lane-1 notch on a mono slot without counting it; `Detector` of lane 1 keeps a stale analysis window when a slot widens 1 → 2 | All three touch files this lane edits, so they are folded in (Tasks 3 and 6). The "restart-drain lane 1" test from that list is delivered as the widen-reset test in Task 3 — the ring residue itself is cleared by the engine's restart cycle (§6.5), the detector window was not. |
+| A-10 | §3.2 `notch_set` fields `rise`, `novelty` | Mapped to the scorer's `rNorm` and `mNorm` (both 0..1). `p_norm`, `asymmetry` and `confirmed_lane` are added so the score can be rebuilt from the log. |
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Audio thread: zero allocation, zero locks, zero logging. **This lane adds no audio-thread code.** If a task finds itself editing `AudioEngine::audioDeviceIOCallbackWithContext` or `NotchChain`, stop.
+- `SessionLogger::log()` and every `EventSink` call may allocate; they run on the detector thread or the message thread, never the audio thread. Neither may ever block on file I/O.
+- The sink is called **only** from `flushEventOutbox()` and **never** while `modelMutex_` is held (D-6).
+- No raw audio, no tester name, no network. Spectra are magnitudes only (D-5).
+- `ctx.ref` is the frame the scorer compared against (`ScoreBreakdown::refFrame`), never a frame looked up by `rise_ms` (D-7).
+- `MainComponent.cpp` must not reference `JUCE_APPLICATION_VERSION_STRING` — it is compiled into `HandsFreeTests` and `HandsFreeSnapshot` without that macro (D-8).
+- Button labels are the ASCII words `GOOD` / `FALSE`; no ✓ ✗ glyphs (memory: mojibake middle dot, 2026-08-25). JUCE 9 trap: `juce::TextButton { "GOOD" }` one argument, never two (memory `juce9-api-traps-2026-08-25`).
+- Every new test states in a comment which production change turns it red (repo convention).
+- Every script that writes a repo file sets UTF-8 explicitly (global rule 6). The logger writes UTF-8, no BOM.
+- Build commands (from the worktree root):
+  ```
+  cmake --build build --config Release
+  cd build && ctest -C Release --output-on-failure -R <Filter>
+  ```
+  A header or `CMakeLists.txt` change needs `cmake -B build -G "Visual Studio 18 2026" -A x64` first. Full-suite gate before every commit that touches `src/`: `ctest -C Release` must report `100% tests passed`. Baseline at plan time: **402/402**.
+- Commit with explicit paths. Never `git add -A`. Do not commit `build/`, `shots/`, `*.log`, or `.superpowers/sdd/.gitignore`.
+- No release from inside a task. Release (`installer\release-alpha.ps1 -Part patch`) happens after the whole-branch review, by the orchestrating session.
